                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Room escape game of good length with very well made puzzles but technical problems especially in object manipulation.\n\nPositive:\n+ difficulty of puzzles is quite high, it is the best immitation of real life room escape games i've seen so far - not just finding objects or codes but really combining multiple sources of information\n+ i like the different locks, interactions are fine (beside rotation locks)\n+ plot and atmosphere of the game is good\n\nNegative:\n- graphics are moderate to simple, especially textures are weak\n- collision of objects from time to time lead to disapearance, resetting is there but i would prefer that this would not be necessary and it introduces additional flaws\n- no saving, so either make it in one run or start over again for the next try\n\nFor this price, i can fully recommend this 3 hour room escape experience with it's high quality of puzzles. It's just a pitty that there are technical porblems.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1491209432,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1491249303,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 9,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6404260396957397,
                        "comment_count": 2,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hello, and thank you for playing A-Escape VR!\n\nI’m planning on going back to Chapter 0 to remake the textures in a higher resolution. I remade a lot of the textures in Chapter 1, but if there are any textures in Chapter 1 I missed let me know and I’ll put them on the list for the next update.\n\nAs for objects disappearing, I’m still working to alleviate the issue. Due to the nature of colliders/rigidbodies it’s difficult to find a solution that doesn’t break the game, but I haven’t given up on it.\n\nChapter 1 is meant to be completed in one hour (and has two endings depending on how quickly you finish) but I’m not completely opposed to the idea of saving. In the meantime I’ll add a way to skip the intro as suggested by ewilson61 for the next update.\n\nAgain, thank you for recommending A-Escape VR. I sincerely apologize that some of the technical hiccups tarnished your overall experience, but I plan to continue updating the game to help alleviate those issues the best I can.\n\nBest regards,\n- Thomas",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1491693729,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
